1
00:00:02,940 --> 00:00:06,260
A MASTER OF NON-VERBAL HUMOR

2
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:14,120
As Victor Hugo once said, laughter is the sun that drives winter from the human phase.

3
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:19,540
And up to now, nobody has been able to do this better than Charlie Chaplin.

4
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:25,000
He brightened the lives of Americans and British through two world wars

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,200
and the hard years in between.

6
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:31,460
He made people laugh at a time when they felt depressed,

7
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:34,680
so they could feel more content with their lives.

8
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:38,000
Not that Charlie’s own life was easy!

9
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:42,080
He was born in a poor family in 1889.

10
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:45,880
His parents were both poor music hall performers.

11
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:52,200
You may find it astonishing that Charlie was taught to sing as soon as he could speak

12
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:54,880
and dance as soon as he could walk.

13
00:00:55,820 --> 00:00:59,960
Such training was common in acting families at this time,

14
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:03,900
especially when the family income was often uncertain.

15
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:09,560
Unfortunately his father died, leaving the family even worse off,

16
00:01:10,140 --> 00:01:14,040
so Charlie spent his childhood looking after his sick mother

17
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:15,000
and his brother.

18
00:01:23,420 --> 00:01:28,040
He could mime and act the fool doing ordinary everyday tasks.

19
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:34,900
No one was ever bored watching him -his subtle acting made everything entertaining.

20
00:01:36,420 --> 00:01:39,620
As time went by, he began making films.

21
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:43,540
He grew more and more popular as his charming character,

22
00:01:43,760 --> 00:01:46,640
the little tramp, became known throughout the world.

23
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:05,680
This character was a social failure but was loved for his optimism

24
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:09,180
and determination to overcome all difficulties.

25
00:02:09,740 --> 00:02:15,260
He was the underdog who was kind even when others were unkind to him.

26
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:20,920
How did the little tramp make a sad situation entertaining?

27
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:25,400
Here is an example from one of his most famous films,

28
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:26,720
The Gold Rush.

29
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:32,740
It is the mid-nineteenth century and gold has just been discovered in California.

30
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:39,020
Like so many others, the little tramp and his friend have rushed there in search of gold,

31
00:02:39,220 --> 00:02:40,740
but without success.

32
00:02:41,660 --> 00:02:47,160
Instead they are hiding in a small hut on the edge of a mountain during a snowstorm

33
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:48,600
with nothing to eat.

34
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:54,320
They are so hungry that they try boiling a pair of leather shoes

35
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:55,200
for their dinner.

36
00:02:56,080 --> 00:03:00,980
Charlie first picks out the laces and eats them as if they were spaghetti.

37
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:06,780
Then he cuts off the leather top of the shoe as if it were the finest steak.

38
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:11,340
Finally he tries cutting and chewing the bottom of the shoe.

39
00:03:12,040 --> 00:03:15,260
He eats each mouthful with great enjoyment.

40
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:22,840
The acting is so convincing that it makes you believe that it is one of the best meals he has ever tasted!

41
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:29,080
Charlie Chaplin wrote, directed and produced the films he starred in.

42
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:35,220
In 1972 he was given a special Oscar for his outstanding work in films.

43
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:40,840
He lived in England and the USA but spent his last years in Switzerland,

44
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:43,560
where he was buried in 1977.

45
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:49,280
He is loved and remembered as a great actor who could inspire people

46
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:50,440
with great confidence.
